<article class="env-lemma" id="056M">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/056M">Lemma <span data-tag="056M">31.5.2</span>.</a> Let $X$ be a scheme. Let $\mathcal{F}$ be a quasi-coherent sheaf on $X$. Let $\mathop{\mathrm{Spec}}(A) = U \subset X$ be an affine open, and set $M = \Gamma (U, \mathcal{F})$. Let $x \in U$, and let $\mathfrak p \subset A$ be the corresponding prime. The following are equivalent </p>
  <p><ol>
  <li><p>
$\mathfrak p$ is weakly associated to $M$, and 
</p>
</li><li><p>
$x$ is weakly associated to $\mathcal{F}$. 
</p>
</li>
</ol></p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      This follows from Algebra, Lemma <a href="/tag/0566" data-tag="0566">10.66.2</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>